WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.460
- [Narrator] Biryani is a
perfectly cooked rice dish,

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:06.160
seasoned with whole spices and
layered between tender chunks

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.900
of meat and streams of delicious gravy.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.520
It's a dish that will give you
the perfect bite each time.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.100
Today we're gonna make our
favorite biryani recipe

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.686
that is sure to keep everyone
you know coming back for more.

00:00:18.686 --> 00:00:21.269
(gentle music)

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.610
The origin of biryani is debatable.

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:27.980
Some say it originated in Iran,

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.390
making its way across
India through trade routes.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:34.170
Others say it originated in Tamil Nadu.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.730
One thing everyone can agree on however

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:38.890
is that biryani is delicious.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:40.670
Almost every region of South Asia

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.586
has their own style of biryani.

00:00:42.586 --> 00:00:46.330
Hyderabad's version is
extra saucy and flavorful.

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:50.810
In Tamil, ambur biryani is made
with mint, yogurt marinade.

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:51.643
And in Lucknow,

00:00:51.643 --> 00:00:54.510
they sometimes use stock
to create a richer flavor.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:57.630
Today we're going to be
making Bombay style biryani.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.880
It's a little sweet and topped
with crispy fried onions.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.440
Let's start with the meat.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:03.880
There are many protein options

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.610
when it comes to making biryani,

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.660
like goat, lamb, shrimp and chicken.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.740
For our recipe, we're going with chicken,

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.510
since it's the most traditional.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:15.200
We're using bone in chicken
thighs and drumsticks.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.640
Boneless chicken works too,

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.890
but bone-in will help to give
us a more flavorful dish.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.530
To incorporate even more
flavor in our chicken,

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.140
we're going to marinate it.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.940
We tested both a spice based marinade

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.580
and a yogurt based marinade.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.410
We found that marinating with yogurt

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:33.530
is key to getting creamy, tender chicken.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.350
So that's what we're going with.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:37.460
Full fat yogurt works best.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.820
In a large bowl, combine the yogurt,

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:41.830
ginger paste, garlic paste,

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:45.390
salt, cumin, coriander, garam masala,

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.370
chili powder and lime juice.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.280
We'll add the chicken
and toss to coat well.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:53.010
Then cover the bowl with
plastic wrap and marinate

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:55.190
for one hour at room temperature

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:58.140
or up to three hours in the refrigerator.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:00.290
Now let's prepare our rice.

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:03.160
For this recipe, we will be using basmati.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.130
It's fragrant, slightly nutty,

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:08.470
and will pair really nicely
with our mix of spices.

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:12.000
We'll start by gently rinsing
the rice in cool water.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.630
Repeat this a few times
until the water runs clear.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:17.720
Now we'll cover the rice with fresh water

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:20.560
and let it soak for 30 to 45 minutes.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.280
Not only does soaking the rice
help to remove excess starch

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:26.250
and speed up the cooking process,

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.090
but for fragrant rice
like basmati and jasmine,

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.850
this will also help strengthen

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.470
their natural aroma and flavors.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:35.660
Once the rice has finished soaking,

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:37.680
we'll move on to the cooking process.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.070
To a pot of water, add cardamom pods,

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:44.230
a cinnamon stick, bay
leaf, cloves and salt.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:47.140
When that comes to a
boil, we'll add our rice.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:50.460
The key to perfectly cooked
biryani is to cook the rice

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.770
until it's only about three
quarters of the way done,

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:55.690
so it's still al dente.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:57.990
This should only take about four minutes.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.030
Drain.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.760
Then add the rice to a
plate or baking sheet

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:05.400
and spread in an even
layer to cool like this.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:06.860
Now that our rice is done,

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:09.330
we can move on to our
next three ingredients

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:12.280
that will make our biryani extra special.

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.810
Onions, prunes and potatoes.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.140
We'll first boil the potatoes separately

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:18.950
until almost tender.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:21.200
If we cooked them with the meat instead,

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:24.270
we'd end up with a mushy
texture in the final dish.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.600
No thanks.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.320
Once our potatoes are softened,

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.410
we're going to fry them in a neutral oil

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:31.600
to provide texture to our dish.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.070
And the crunch doesn't stop there.

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:36.340
Next, we're gonna fry some onions.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:39.620
A must when it comes to
Bombay style biryani.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:43.280
We recommend using a small
red onion or shallot.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.270
We'll fry them until they're
nice and golden brown.

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:49.920
Seriously, look how good those look.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.110
Before we move on to layering our biryani,

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:54.590
we're going to make some saffron water.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:56.860
Saffron adds a luxurious scent,

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:59.337
flavor and color to our biryani.

00:03:59.337 --> 00:04:01.270
We know it can be pricey,

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:03.390
so if you don't have saffron on hand,

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:06.520
use turmeric to get that orange hue.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:09.494
We're going to pour hot water
over our saffron threads.

00:04:09.494 --> 00:04:12.570
And then gently crush them
with the back of a spoon

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:15.070
to get all of that flavor out.

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:17.150
Now let's make our gravy.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.800
We tested a few different
oils for our gravy

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:23.710
and found that a mixture of oil
and ghee or clarified butter

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:27.400
creates the best flavor
without being too rich.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.200
We'll heat our oil
mixture until it shimmers.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.880
Then we're going to add
all of our whole spices

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:36.140
to get every last drop
of flavor out of them.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:39.390
We want to fry them until
they are fragrant, not burnt,

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:41.600
about one to two minutes.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:45.000
Then we'll add our
chopped onions and saute.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.010
Once the onions begin to brown,

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.980
add the tomatoes and cook
for three to five minutes.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:54.160
Then add the marinated chicken,
a splash of water and salt.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.820
Cover and let this cook for 10 minutes.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:58.660
We'll add the potatoes back in

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:02.300
and then add our special
ingredient, prunes.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.310
Prunes are used in Bombay style biryani

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:07.647
to add an element of
sweetness to the dish.

00:05:07.647 --> 00:05:11.280
Now that our gravy is finished,
let's move on to layering.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.940
When it comes to cooking biryani,

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:14.770
there are a few ways to do it.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:16.510
You can cook it dum-style.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:18.850
which involves layering raw ingredients

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:23.270
in a heavy bottomed pot and
slow cooking them all together.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:25.710
Or you can make it pukka-style,

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:28.730
which means cooking all of
the components separately

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:31.660
and then layering them together after.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:33.900
We're cooking our biryani pukka-style,

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.560
because it's more traditional
for Bombay style biryani,

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.030
and it ensures we don't
overcook any of the elements

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:40.910
in the dish.

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:43.990
We'll start by reserving
half of the beautiful gravy

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:47.460
and add half of our rice into the pot.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:51.330
Then we'll sprinkle some of
our saffron water on top.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.850
We'll add some herbs, a little ghee,

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.290
and our fried onions as finishing touches

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.860
for the first layer.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:59.840
And then we'll repeat the whole process

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.590
for the second layer.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.520
Once we have our biryani all piled up,

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:06.670
we're going to cover the pot with foil

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:09.290
and seal it really tightly.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:11.770
Traditionally, we'd
wrap the rim with dough

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:14.220
to get the tight seal we're looking for,

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.630
but today we're gonna keep
it simple by using foil.

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:20.210
Once it's done cooking, we'll
leave it covered to rest

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:23.770
for 10 minutes to let the
steam really fluff up the rice

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.200
and finish cooking.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.780
And there you have it,

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.890
your beautifully layered Bombay biryani.

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:32.780
With biryani, every bit of time taken

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:35.670
to perfect this dish really pays off.

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:37.700
We're going to serve our biryani today

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:40.690
with a little onion
raita and pickled mango.

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:43.550
We know that nothing will
beat your moms biryani,

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:46.843
but we think this recipe comes very close.

00:06:47.727 --> 00:06:50.310
(gentle music)

